; MM-EXEC-6c through a callee written without a signature. `pong` has
; none, so its type comes from its body, and it is defined above `ping`
; because a call to it from above would need one (AX3089). Its `define`
; still takes exactly its two parameters, so the prototypes match and
; both calls are `musttail`: ten million alternating calls run in
; constant stack at every `--opt` (the `.optstable` beside this file).
;
; The emitter used to read the callee's arity from its signature
; alone, so the call into `pong` stayed a plain call. That died by
; SIGSEGV at `--opt 0` and answered at `--opt 2`, where LLVM's
; sibling-call pass flattened it (fuzz mutant m02641 of
; tests/stdlib/467-mutual-tail.ax, seed 20260927).
(import IO)

(:: ping (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (pong i acc)
  (if (>= i 10000000)
    acc
    (ping (+ i 1) (+ acc 1))))

(fn (ping i acc)
  (if (>= i 10000000)
    acc
    (pong (+ i 1) (+ acc 1))))

(:: main Int)
;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  {
    (println (ping 0 0))
    0
  })
